CP
==

Copy files or folders.


BASIC
-----
cp original.txt copy.txt

Creates a copy of the file.


OPTIONS
-------
Copy folder and contents:
  cp -r folder backup

Preserve permissions:
  cp -p file.txt copy.txt

Both combined:
  cp -rp original backup


WHAT IT DOES
------------
• Creates exact copy
• Original stays unchanged
• New file is independent


COPY TO FOLDER
---------------
cp file.txt folder/

Copies file into folder.
Keeps same name.


ERRORS
------
"file exists"       → Destination exists
"no such file"      → Original doesn't exist
"permission denied" → No write access
